  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "From announcement to closing roster",
      "sourceIds": [
        "person-keith-tyser-identity-0",
        "person-mark-barney-identity-0",
        "person-son-pham-identity-0",
        "dispatch-2026-10-18-arc3-superteam-merger-official",
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Keith Tyser’s ARC Slayers and the former Son & Mark & Ronen entry now appear together as Team Turducken. The closing public board lists all seven accounts under entry 15605182: dzjiann, keithtyser, markbarney, mitubant, ngyzly, scizical and sonphamorg. The team is fifth at 48.92, unchanged since the previous close. The merger changes the roster; these observations do not establish a scoring benefit. The official announcement leads this issue above the recap. Mark Barney, the Digest’s head human editor, is a member of the merged team."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Two leaders keep the high ground",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs leads at 68.91, with Yi-Chia Chen second at 67.49: a 1.42-point gap, unchanged since the previous close. Third-placed mtg has 50.37 and the last dance is fourth at 49.85, leaving the newly combined fifth-place team close to those two challengers but still well behind the leading pair. The public board remains provisional; the illustration’s citadels and machinery are sporting metaphors, not evidence of equipment or spending."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Eight workshops, an unchanged top ten",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-identity-0",
        "person-grigoriy-zatravkin-identity-0",
        "person-richard-csaky-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tonight’s High Ground panorama brings the eight chasing entries into one scene. Behind Team Turducken, 復活の混テキスト holds sixth, Grigoriy Zatravkin seventh and Majkel1337 eighth. NVARC3, whose observed roster includes Jean-François Puget and Ivan Sorokin, is ninth; artificialagencylab.com completes the ten. All ten closing ranks and scores match the previous close. The seven Turducken characters and two Yorkies are approved editorial avatars; the anonymous builders in other camps do not represent roster headcounts."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The chase below gold",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-18-1002-arc-3-two-teams-leap-into-top-hundred",
        "wire-2026-10-18-1603-arc-3-leszek-gora-jumps-to-thirty-fifth",
        "wire-2026-10-18-1603-arc-3-the-agi-boys-rise-to-forty-second"
      ],
      "text": "Leszek Góra supplies the afternoon’s sharpest high-field move: the wire recorded a 7.05-point score step to 35.96, and he closes 35th. The AGI Boys finish 42nd at 35.35 after their recorded 4.79-point step. Both remain below the 38.20 score at the last of 18 provisional gold places. Earlier wire movers Matt #2 and Tecnod8.AI close 48th and 54th. Rustam Bazarbayev finishes 86th, up 210 places and 2.04 points against the previous close; that is a different comparison from the rank change at the instant his score event was recorded."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A separate puzzle benchmark takes shape",
      "sourceIds": [
        "social-2111842926917550193"
      ],
      "text": "Beyond the Kaggle race, Psyho says a nearly finished private PuzzleScript benchmark selects 40 games from more than 300. That is the author’s announcement of an independent project, not an official new ARC competition. Its scores, logs and eventual release remain unverified by this desk."
    }
  ],
